  "layoutMapUrl": null,
  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 4 is the most famous hole in Fort Worth disc golf: 755 feet of par 3 that rolls downhill and demands the biggest drive you have — twice. It's a hole that shouldn't be a par 3, which is exactly why everyone loves it. Par here is a badge that gets you respect in the DFW scene.",
  "localTips": "Hole 4 is a 755-foot par 3 — bring your longest driver and don't be ashamed of a layup. The creek is in play on four of the last five holes, so the back stretch is where rounds come apart. Free to play; the course has real elevation and heavy trees.",
